phi-adapter-hue (0.0~git202609081825.71c2a25-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Rebuilt without Qt on the SDK loop client: the poll as non-blocking
    requests, the event stream as a stream.
  * The bridge certificate is verified against Signify root, installed as
    /usr/share/phi/adapters/hue/huebridge_cacert.pem, and must name the
    bridge id. It was not verified at all.
  * A poll that could not fetch a resource type keeps its channels from
    the last poll that could. Treating it as empty made phi-core remove
    and recreate the dials button channels - the button that vanished
    from the app.
  * The bridge is a Gateway, not a Sensor.
  * Commands answer with the bridge answer; devices and values are sent
    only when they changed; a click is a single or a double, never both.
  * Depends on phi-adapter-sdk (>= 0.13.0); no longer on Qt6 or
    phi-adapter-sdk-qt.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 18:25:33 +0200

